              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Mounting Cameras Too High</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Twelve feet up looks tidy and produces footage of the top of a head. Seven to eight feet, angled so people walk toward the lens, produces footage of a face — which is the entire point. Resist the urge to mount at the height the ladder happens to reach.
              </p>
